- the stale "Orca's sandbox" comment in `claude-main-edit-guard.sh`.

Waiting on the round-6 correctness reviewer before editing.

Round 7, security+quality: no Critical, one Important. The GUI no longer gets a GTK runtime environment (GSettings schemas, pixbuf loaders), which the bwrap env used to supply. If no portal file chooser is running, Chromium falls back to GTK's own chooser, and that needs the host's `org.gtk.Settings.FileChooser` schema or it aborts. Nothing tests that.

`wrapGAppsHook3` would leak `XDG_DATA_DIRS` and friends into every child, the same problem as nixGL. Instead I'll add a test that nixpkgs' GLib, running in the app's own environment, can read that schema from the host. I'll also record the trade-off in the comment.

